alwaysApply: true
---

Every implementation should be written as if the application will be deployed for a live hackathon demonstration. 
ENSURE IT WORKS AND IS HOSTABLE ON RAILWAY AND VERCEL

Avoid shortcuts that only work in development.

Prefer production-quality implementations over mocked UI.

Use realistic data models.

Use modular services.

Keep APIs reusable.

Ensure the application remains deployable throughout development.

Whenever third-party APIs are unavailable, build clean abstraction layers so real services can be connected later without rewriting business logic.

The final demo should appear to judges as a working enterprise banking security platform rather than a prototype.

When implementing major features, prioritize:

• Stability
• Scalability
• Realistic workflows
• Professional UI
• Explainability
• Live interaction
• Robust architecture

Do not implement features solely for visual demonstration.

Every visible feature should be backed by meaningful application logic.
